# GreenThreads Denver Store #13 — HR Portfolio

**Yasmine Lopez | HR Operations Liaison | AI.205: AI Integration in Business I**

This portfolio documents one quarter of applying AI to a real operating problem: staffing
GreenThreads' Denver Store #13 within a 90-day launch window, without adding corporate
headcount. It moves from functional analysis, to document and data investigation, to a working,
tested AI assistant, to an executive brief recommending action — one throughline, four
deliverables.

## The Story

Denver's 14-person floor team needed to be built fast, and Sales Associate — the highest-turnover
role and 8 of the 14 seats — was the bottleneck. Cross-referencing the Employee Handbook, offer
letters, and 148 applicant records showed GreenThreads wasn't following its own written pay
policy for this role, and applicant data confirmed the real cost: pay was the single most common
reason candidates declined. A custom AI assistant was built and adversarially tested so HR could
keep checking these numbers without a one-off analysis each time — and the resulting executive
brief recommends a phased pay correction, while explicitly naming what Finance still needs to
confirm before the full fix is guaranteed.

